{"id":"mahabharata-3-167","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":167,"title":"सप्तषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 167 · Arjuna fights the Nivatakavachas","summary":{"en":"Thousands of demons assail Arjuna, and he cuts them down with his arrows as Matali drives the chariot through their ranks. The survivors turn to magic, raining down weapons and vanishing from sight.","kn":"ಸಾವಿರಾರು ದಾನವರು ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಮೇಲೆರಗುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಮಾತಲಿ ರಥವನ್ನು ಅವರ ಪಂಕ್ತಿಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ನಡೆಸುವಾಗ ಅವನು ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಕೆಡವುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಉಳಿದವರು ಮಾಯೆಯನ್ನಾಶ್ರಯಿಸಿ ಆಯುಧಮಳೆಗರೆದು ಕಣ್ಮರೆಯಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"हज़ारों दानव अर्जुन पर टूट पड़ते हैं, और मातलि के उनकी पंक्तियों के बीच रथ दौड़ाते समय वे बाणों से उन्हें काट गिराते हैं। बचे हुए दानव माया का सहारा लेकर अस्त्र बरसाते और अदृश्य हो जाते हैं।","te":"వేలాది దానవులు అర్జునునిపై విరుచుకుపడతారు, మాతలి వారి వరుసల మధ్య రథాన్ని నడుపుతుండగా అతడు బాణాలతో వారిని కూల్చుతాడు. మిగిలినవారు మాయను ఆశ్రయించి ఆయుధవర్షం కురిపించి అదృశ్యమవుతారు.","ta":"ஆயிரக்கணக்கான அசுரர்கள் அர்ஜுனனைத் தாக்க, மாதலி அவர்கள் அணிகளுக்கிடையே தேரைச் செலுத்தும்போது அவன் அம்புகளால் அவர்களை வீழ்த்துகிறான். எஞ்சியோர் மாயையைக் கைக்கொண்டு ஆயுத மழை பொழிந்து மறைகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ആയിരക്കണക്കിന് രാക്ഷസന്മാർ അർജുനനെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; മാതലി അവരുടെ നിരകൾക്കിടയിലൂടെ തേര് തെളിക്കുമ്പോൾ അദ്ദേഹം അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് അവരെ വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു. അതിജീവിച്ചവർ മായാവിദ്യയിലേക്ക് തിരിയുന്നു; ആയുധവർഷം ചൊരിഞ്ഞ് അവർ കണ്ണിൽനിന്ന് മറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.167; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो निवातकवचाः सर्वे वेगेन भारत ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्मां सहिताः प्रगृहीतायुधा रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Nivatakavachas, O Bharata, rushed at me together with great speed, weapons in hand."}},{"n":2,"text":"आच्छिद्य रथपन्थानमुत्क्रोशन्तो महारथाः ।\nआवृत्य सर्वतस्ते मां शरवर्षैरवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those great warriors blocked my chariot's path, shouting, and surrounded me on every side, showering me with arrows."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततोऽपरे महावीर्याः शूलपट्टिशपाणयः ।\nशूलानि च भुशुण्डीश्च मुमुचुर्दानवा मयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then other mighty danavas, with spears and pattishas in their hands, hurled spears and bhushundis at me."}},{"n":4,"text":"तच्छूलवर्षं सुमहद्गदाशक्तिसमाकुलम् ।\nअनिशं सृज्यमानं तैरपतन्मद्रथोपरि ॥","meaning":{"en":"That huge rain of spears, mixed with maces and darts, poured down without pause onto my chariot."}},{"n":5,"text":"अन्ये मामभ्यधावन्त निवातकवचा युधि ।\nशितशस्त्रायुधा रौद्राः कालरूपाः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other Nivatakavachas ran at me in the battle, fierce strikers like death itself, with sharp blades and weapons."}},{"n":6,"text":"तानहं विविधैर्बाणैर्वेगवद्भिरजिह्मगैः ।\nगाण्डीवमुक्तैरभ्यघ्नमेकैकं दशभिर्मृधे ।\nते कृता विमुखाः सर्वे मत्प्रयुक्तैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I struck each of them down with ten swift, straight-flying arrows of many kinds loosed from the Gandiva. Those arrows, sharpened on stone, turned them all away from me."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो मातलिना तूर्णं हयास्ते संप्रचोदिताः ।\nरथमार्गाद्बहूंस्तत्र विचेरुर्वातरंहसः ।\nसुसंयता मातलिना प्रामथ्नन्त दितेः सुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Matali quickly urged the horses on, and they roamed with the speed of the wind along many tracks of the field. Well held in by Matali, they trampled the sons of Diti."}},{"n":8,"text":"शतं शतास्ते हरयस्तस्मिन्युक्ता महारथे ।\nतदा मातलिना यत्ता व्यचरन्नल्पका इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred times a hundred horses seemed yoked to that great chariot, yet under Matali's control they moved as if they were only a few."}},{"n":9,"text":"तेषां चरणपातेन रथनेमिस्वनेन च ।\nमम बाणनिपातैश्च हतास्ते शतशोऽसुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the fall of their hooves, the rumble of the chariot wheels and the strike of my arrows, those asuras were slain by the hundred."}},{"n":10,"text":"गतासवस्तथा चान्ये प्रगृहीतशरासनाः ।\nहतसारथयस्तत्र व्यकृष्यन्त तुरंगमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, lifeless, with bows still in hand and their charioteers killed, were dragged along by their horses."}},{"n":11,"text":"ते दिशो विदिशः सर्वाः प्रतिरुध्य प्रहारिणः ।\nनिघ्नन्ति विविधैः शस्त्रैस्ततो मे व्यथितं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blocking every direction and intermediate direction, the attackers struck me with many weapons, and my mind was troubled."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततोऽहं मातलेर्वीर्यमपश्यं परमाद्भुतम् ।\nअश्वांस्तथा वेगवतो यदयत्नादधारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I saw Matali's extraordinary prowess, in how he held in those swift horses without effort."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततोऽहं लघुभिश्चित्रैरस्त्रैस्तानसुरान्रणे ।\nसायुधानच्छिनं राजञ्शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with light and varied weapons I cut down those asuras and their arms by the hundred and the thousand, O king."}},{"n":14,"text":"एवं मे चरतस्तत्र सर्वयत्नेन शत्रुहन् ।\nप्रीतिमानभवद्वीरो मातलिः शक्रसारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As I fought there with all my effort, slayer of foes, the hero Matali, Indra's charioteer, grew pleased."}},{"n":15,"text":"वध्यमानास्ततस्ते तु हयैस्तेन रथेन च ।\nअगमन्प्रक्षयं केचिन्न्यवर्तन्त तथापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by the horses, the chariot and me, some of them perished while others turned back."}},{"n":16,"text":"स्पर्धमाना इवास्माभिर्निवातकवचा रणे ।\nशरवर्षैर्महद्भिर्मां समन्तात्प्रत्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As if vying with us, the Nivatakavachas in the battle checked me from all sides with great showers of arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततोऽहं लघुभिश्चित्रैर्ब्रह्मास्त्रपरिमन्त्रितैः ।\nव्यधमं सायकैराशु शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with light, varied arrows consecrated with the Brahma weapon I swiftly destroyed them by the hundred and the thousand."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः संपीड्यमानास्ते क्रोधाविष्टा महासुराः ।\nअपीडयन्मां सहिताः शरशूलासिवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hard pressed, those great asuras were seized with rage and together pressed me hard with rains of arrows, spears and swords."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततोऽहमस्त्रमातिष्ठं परमं तिग्मतेजसम् ।\nदयितं देवराजस्य माधवं नाम भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I took up the supreme weapon of fierce energy named Madhava, dear to the king of the gods, O Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः खड्गांस्त्रिशूलांश्च तोमरांश्च सहस्रशः ।\nअस्त्रवीर्येण शतधा तैर्मुक्तानहमच्छिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the power of that weapon I cut into a hundred pieces the thousands of swords, tridents and javelins they hurled."}},{"n":21,"text":"छित्त्वा प्रहरणान्येषां ततस्तानपि सर्वशः ।\nप्रत्यविध्यमहं रोषाद्दशभिर्दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After cutting their weapons, I pierced them all over in anger with ten arrows each."}},{"n":22,"text":"गाण्डीवाद्धि तदा संख्ये यथा भ्रमरपङ्क्तयः ।\nनिष्पतन्ति तथा बाणास्तन्मातलिरपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrows streamed from the Gandiva in that battle like lines of bees, and Matali praised it."}},{"n":23,"text":"तेषामपि तु बाणास्ते बहुत्वाच्छलभा इव ।\nअवाकिरन्मां बलवत्तानहं व्यधमं शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their arrows too, so many that they were like swarms of locusts, fell thickly on me, but I destroyed them with my arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"वध्यमानास्ततस्ते तु निवातकवचाः पुनः ।\nशरवर्षैर्महद्भिर्मां समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down, the Nivatakavachas again surrounded me on every side with great showers of arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"शरवेगान्निहत्याहमस्त्रैः शरविघातिभिः ।\nज्वलद्भिः परमैः शीघ्रैस्तानविध्यं सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beating back their arrow-rush with weapons that break arrows, blazing, supreme and swift, I pierced them by the thousand."}},{"n":26,"text":"तेषां छिन्नानि गात्राणि विसृजन्ति स्म शोणितम् ।\nप्रावृषीवातिवृष्टानि शृङ्गाणीव धराभृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their cut limbs poured blood, like the peaks of mountains drenched in the rains."}},{"n":27,"text":"इन्द्राशनिसमस्पर्शैर्वेगवद्भिरजिह्मगैः ।\nमद्बाणैर्वध्यमानास्ते समुद्विग्नाः स्म दानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by my swift, straight arrows, whose touch was like Indra's thunderbolt, those danavas were thrown into panic."}},{"n":28,"text":"शतधा भिन्नदेहान्त्राः क्षीणप्रहरणौजसः ।\nततो निवातकवचा मामयुध्यन्त मायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their bodies and entrails torn into a hundred pieces, and the strength of their weapons spent, the Nivatakavachas then fought me by sorcery."}}]}]}